spes: textures over the planes of a planar IOSurface (flame patch 0003).

newTextureWithDescriptor:iosurface:plane: returned nil for any surface with planes. The 420f surfaces (SpringBoard's
787x1705 and 1125x2436 app snapshots, CollectionsPoster's previews, assetsd thumbnails: 214 of them in one boot) then
had no textures, and CoreAnimation's YCbCr pass drew magenta with black specks: Safari's tab overview and its card in the
switcher. Each plane now gets a texture over the one import of the whole allocation, at the plane's offset with its rows
(the runtime's IoSurfacePlane, tested in metal2vulkan-validation ycbcr_textures.rs); iosurfacePlane answers the plane.

